# Logging System

**ALWAYS check the log file when debugging any issue:**
`~/Library/Application Support/com.meridian.app/logs/meridian.log`

Read this file FIRST before forming hypotheses. It contains timestamped, categorized output from every subsystem. The log captures stderr from Wine processes, exit codes, phase timings, and error details that are not visible in the Xcode console.

Meridian writes structured, timestamped logs to plain text files in addition to the macOS unified log (Xcode console). This enables post-mortem debugging without Xcode attached.

## Log File Locations

| File | Path |
|------|------|
| **Current session** | `~/Library/Application Support/com.meridian.app/logs/meridian.log` |
| **Previous session** | `~/Library/Application Support/com.meridian.app/logs/meridian-previous.log` |

At every app launch, `meridian.log` is renamed to `meridian-previous.log` (one generation kept), and a fresh `meridian.log` is created. This means the current session's log is always in `meridian.log`.

The log directory is created automatically on first launch. Files are flushed after every write, so they survive crashes.

## Reading Logs

**In Settings:** Settings → Updates → Diagnostics → "Open Log" button opens `meridian.log` in the system default text editor.

**In Terminal:**
```bash
# Tail the live log while the app runs
tail -f ~/Library/Application\ Support/com.meridian.app/logs/meridian.log

# Grep for errors only
grep ERROR ~/Library/Application\ Support/com.meridian.app/logs/meridian.log

# Grep for Steam bootstrap failures
grep -E "healthMonitor|waitUntilReady|BOOTSTRAP" ~/Library/Application\ Support/com.meridian.app/logs/meridian.log

# Full absolute path (for AI tools reading the file directly)
# /Users/<username>/Library/Application Support/com.meridian.app/logs/meridian.log
```

**From AI/Cursor:** Read the file directly with the Read tool using the absolute path — the log is plain UTF-8 text.

## Log Format

Each line:
```
2026-03-27 14:32:05 CDT  [INFO]  [WineSteamManager] [startPersistent] pid=47788
2026-03-27 14:32:06 CDT  [WARN]  [BootstrapManager] [bootstrap] Steam failed to start
2026-03-27 14:32:06 CDT  [ERROR] [WineSteamManager] [healthMonitor] Steam died — uptime=4s exitCode=1 reason=normal-exit retry=1/5
```

Format: `<ISO-8601 timestamp>  [LEVEL]  [Category] <message>`

Levels: `INFO`, `DEBUG`, `WARN`, `ERROR`

## Startup Header

Every log begins with a diagnostic header block:
```
================================================================================
Meridian v1.0.3 (Build 42)  —  started 2026-03-27 14:32:05 CDT
macOS 15.4.0 | arm64
Application Support: /Users/nick/Library/Application Support/com.meridian.app/
Log: /Users/nick/Library/Application Support/com.meridian.app/logs/meridian.log
================================================================================
```

## Implementation

All logging goes through `MeridianLog` (`Meridian/Utilities/MeridianLog.swift`), which simultaneously writes to:
- `os.Logger` (macOS unified log, visible in Xcode console and `log stream`)
- `LogFileWriter.shared` (the on-disk file, via a dedicated serial `DispatchQueue`)

**Replacing a logger in a new file:**
```swift
// Old:
private let log = Logger(subsystem: "com.meridian.app", category: "MyComponent")

// New:
private let log = MeridianLog(category: "MyComponent")
```

Call sites are identical: `log.info(...)`, `log.warning(...)`, `log.error(...)`, `log.debug(...)`. Plain `String` interpolation only — no `privacy:` annotations needed.

